{
  "summary": "The image-only, single-profile ResNet50 baseline achieved a validation accuracy of 0.2079 and F1 of 0.1718, lower than the previously completed RNA-only PCA baseline with 0.4849 accuracy and 0.4639 F1. This suggests that, in this simple configuration, image features provide weaker validation predictive signal than the RNA baseline, but the comparison does not isolate image modality from the choice of encoder. It remains uncertain whether the low result reflects limited image signal, an inadequate ResNet50 representation, or the single-profile setting."
}

